      "id": "https://www.thepoultrysite.com/news/2026/11/farmer-sentiment-improves-in-october-on-government-payments",
      "url": "https://www.thepoultrysite.com/news/2026/11/farmer-sentiment-improves-in-october-on-government-payments",
      "title": "[thepoultrysite.com] U.S. farmer sentiment rises to 126 as USDA payments roll out",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://kagiproxy.com/img/nwvdV6mHFYK6k51wevI2cF3zBfYtq7VJeegs0uXAfHINCv8me4R0y2R4wsKL2n-3krGDfvXebBxFpqSXQKLNk34YHsVscggui0OAG5SZVvoQPaSefdcpOQfR8mT3zVKHl7wqKnLSeg7YH8qLX2uXY_lDL4kxDQ\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\nU.S. farmer sentiment rose to 126 in October from 123 in September as the U.S. Department of Agriculture distributed Agriculture Risk Coverage and Price Loss Coverage payments. The survey did not ask farmers whether the payments affected their responses, so the timing does not establish that the payments caused the increase.\n\nThe Purdue University-CME Group Ag Economy Barometer survey of 400 farmers found that current conditions improved, but future expectations slipped two points as high input costs remained the leading concern. Respondents were less confident about tariffs and the country’s direction, while one in five said it was a good time to invest in machinery and buildings.",
